Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('67a9f930e3f734134b50db0e67f88e3dc03d2341ed6b9be9006e7089896a6f72',), event=Revised(decision='publishedplaintext', at=datetime(2026, 11, 16, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='Every published byte is plain text both checks read, or admitted by digest: at a terminal, or by drawing its store again', body="*Every published byte is plain text both checks read, or admitted* (2026-10-10, the owner: hand-rolled decoders are an arms race a filter loses): secrets are gitleaks's (`scripts/secret-rules.toml`, a fixture key by fingerprint in `.gitleaksignore`); the matcher reads words and decodes nothing; a file it cannot read (a binary, a base64 or hex run, a quoted-printable body, an SVG image) or a fingerprinted one is a hit until `scripts/public-admitted.sha256` lists its path and digest, a line `train.sh publish --admit` takes at a terminal, as it takes a new fingerprint or a change to the rules. `public-scan.sh` runs the same guard over every commit of a Prodrome range, and admits a public store's pictures (`roadmap.svg`, `roadmap-dark.svg`) where drawing the store at their commit again (`prodrome draw --admissions`) gives their bytes (2026-11-16, door 2): their words are then the words of objects door 1 has read. `-t 0` stops cron and land, not a shell (SECURITY.md).", rationale="The owner, 2026-10-10: hand-rolled decoders are an arms race a filter loses. 2026-11-16: typst draws glyphs as outlines, so no guard reads a picture's words; a redraw is the only reader, and without it every push would need an admission at a terminal.", supersedes=()))